// Reference answer for GUML-Bench task `l02-changelog`.
//
// Content-heavy and entirely `core`: no state, no requests, nothing to hydrate. The compression figure
// for this category is expected to be the lowest of the six, and the reason is visible here — most of
// these lines are release notes, and prose is incompressible.

page Changelog title="Meridian changelog" description="Every release of Meridian, newest first." lang=en

nav Meridian
  link Releases #releases
  link Docs /docs

section #releases
  h1 Changelog
  p Every release of Meridian, newest first. Breaking changes carry their migration note on the entry that introduces them, so you never have to read two pages to upgrade one version.

section "July 2026"
  card "1.6.0 — Concurrent replica promotion"
    note Released 24 July 2026
    badge Breaking danger
    p Promoting a read replica no longer drains the primary first. Promotion now completes in under two seconds on a 400 GB volume, against roughly ninety seconds before.
    note Replicas created before 1.6 must be re-registered once with `meridian replica adopt`. Promotion of an unadopted replica refuses rather than falling back.
  card "1.5.2 — Planner estimates for partial indexes"
    note Released 9 July 2026
    badge Fix
    p The planner treated a partial index as covering the whole relation, so a query with a matching predicate was costed as a sequential scan and often got one. Estimates now use the index predicate's selectivity.

divider

section "June 2026"
  card "1.5.1 — Connection pool no longer leaks on cancelled statements"
    note Released 27 June 2026
    badge Fix
    p A statement cancelled between planning and execution left its pooled connection checked out. A busy analytics workload exhausted a pool of fifty in about four hours.
  card "1.5.0 — Point-in-time restore to a second"
    note Released 12 June 2026
    badge Feature primary
    p Restore targets are now expressed to the second rather than to the nearest write-ahead-log segment, so recovering from a bad migration no longer costs the writes either side of it.

divider

section "May 2026"
  card "1.4.1 — Correct row counts after a rolled-back COPY"
    note Released 29 May 2026
    badge Fix
    p A `COPY` that failed part-way left the relation's row estimate at the post-copy figure until the next analyse, which skewed every plan chosen in between.
  card "1.4.0 — Logical replication to a second region"
    note Released 6 May 2026
    badge Feature primary
    p A publication can now target a subscriber in another region without a bridging instance. Lag is reported per subscription in the console rather than only in the logs.

footer "© 2026 Meridian Data — every release is also tagged in the repository."
  link Docs /docs
  link Status /status
